      "writtenOn": "2021-10-08T11:50:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, it wouldn\u0027t be straightforward to do so.\n\n`AndroidMkData` allows writing Make entries as a string using a custom function (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/androidmk.go;l\u003d73;drc\u003d65ee90a362234edc6b9dbe3d43eaa1f923aadc47), while `AndroidMkEntries` only allows writing entries in a more structured way (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/android/androidmk.go;l\u003d134;drc\u003dmaster). As an example, you can see how `AndroidMkData` is written in apex.go (https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/apex/androidmk.go;l\u003d355;drc\u003d7c02e26cbaddb61bde74ac5888b912f3205b7297).\n\nBecause of this, `AndroidMkData` and `AndroidMkEntries` are tested in completely different ways. A test against `AndroidMkData` usually checks whether the constructed string contains certain substrings or not, while a test against `AndroidMkEntries` can check the entries in a fine granularity with `EntryMap`. You can see the difference in the tests here and below.\n\nIf we added a function to help test both `AndroidMkData` and `AndroidMkEntries`, the function would have to provide a unified way to represent the entries - either as a string or in a structured way. However, neither way is ideal. If we represented the entries as a string, tests would lose the ability to check the entries in a fine granularity. On the other hand, if we chose to represent the entries in a structured way, it would be tricky to convert the string generated by custom functions in `AndroidMkData` into the structure. The conversion would be error-prone because there can always be edge cases.",
      "parentUuid": "1c181873_53da9759",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8464,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 8464,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "0dac924c78ce95a81f78e77dae73e9980889c8be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
