      "writtenOn": "2021-10-12T03:27:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the suggestions. In fact, AndroidMkData is usually a complicated string. The form of the string is something like below:\n\ninclude $(CLEAR_VARS)\nSOME_VAR :\u003d xxx\nSOME_VAR +\u003d xxx\nSOME_OTHER_VAR :\u003d xxx\ninclude xxx\n\ninclude $(CLEAR_VARS)\nSOME_VAR :\u003d xxx\nSOME_VAR +\u003d xxx\nSOME_OTHER_VAR :\u003d xxx\ninclude xxx\n\nThe challenge is that it contains multiple Make modules, and there isn\u0027t a clean way to tell the boundary between modules. In addition, there are other operators such as \"+\u003d\" that need to be handled. Therefore simply splitting on newlines and \":\u003d\" won\u0027t work. Potentially, we can implement a parser that covers most of the cases, but due to the reasons above, even the simplest one requires non-trivial work.\n\nOn the other hand, joining the contents of AndroidMkEntries into a single string doesn\u0027t allow users to check the entries in a fine granularity as I said before, so I can hardly imagine any user that would want that.\n\nSince `AndroidMkData` is deprecated anyway, adding a helper function that works for both data structures doesn\u0027t yield much return IMO. I\u0027ll leave it as is for now.",
      "parentUuid": "289b007b_7be65e1b",
